8. STRICT ROLE + STATE + DISTRICT FILTERING
========================================

Create one shared data model for all services:

type RoleKey =
  | "student"
  | "farmer"
  | "worker"
  | "senior"
  | "disability";

interface LocalizedText {
  en: string;
  kn: string;
  hi: string;
  ta: string;
  te: string;
  ml: string;
  mr: string;
  bn: string;
  gu: string;
  pa: string;
  or: string;
  ur: string;
  as: string;
}

interface ServiceItem {
  id: string;
  role: RoleKey;
  states: string[] | "ALL";
  districts?: string[] | "ALL";
  category?: string[];
  incomeLevel?: string[];
  title: LocalizedText;
  department: LocalizedText;
  benefit: LocalizedText;
  eligibility: LocalizedText;
  documents: LocalizedText[];
  deadline?: LocalizedText;
  tags: LocalizedText[];
  applyMode: "IN_APP_FORM" | "OFFICIAL_PORTAL";
  verified: boolean;
}

Use this exact filtering logic in every feature:

items.filter(item =>
  item.role === userProfile.role &&
  (item.states === "ALL" || item.states.includes(userProfile.state)) &&
  (item.districts === "ALL" || !item.districts || item.districts.includes(userProfile.district))
);

Apply this same filter to:
- My Next Steps tasks
- Service Directory schemes
- Document Vault documents
- AssistFill forms
- Consent Centre requests
- Human Support contacts
- AI Guide suggestion chips
- Home quick-action cards

Never show mixed-role schemes.

Reset custom tasks, selected forms, and chat suggestions whenever role, state, or district changes.

